---
title: "Link"
eyebrow: "Components"
lead: "A text link is bold and underlined, so it never depends on color alone to look like a link."
permalink: /components/link/
---
{% from "components.njk" import textLink %}
<section aria-labelledby="text-h">
  <h2 id="text-h" class="type-h2">Text link</h2>
  <p>Body SemiBold with a 1px underline. Hover and press change the underline to 2px and shift the color. The target is 32px tall.</p>
  {% demo "Text link and external link" %}
  {{ textLink("Read the case study", "#") }}
  {{ textLink("Open the resume", "#", external=true) }}
  {% enddemo %}
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="ext-h">
  <h2 id="ext-h" class="type-h2">External links</h2>
  <p>A link that opens a new tab shows the external-link icon and carries hidden "(opens in new tab)" text for screen readers. It uses <code>rel="noopener"</code>.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="brand-h">
  <h2 id="brand-h" class="type-h2">On a blue surface</h2>
  {% demo "Link on brand", "brand" %}
  {{ textLink("Get in touch", "#", onBrand=true) }}
  {% enddemo %}
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="use-h">
  <h2 id="use-h" class="type-h2">Using links</h2>
  <div class="rules">
    <div class="rule"><h3 class="type-h3">Do</h3><ul>
      <li>Say where the link goes: "Read the case study", not "Click here".</li>
      <li>Keep the underline.</li>
    </ul></div>
    <div class="rule"><h3 class="type-h3">Don't</h3><ul>
      <li>Remove the underline and rely on color.</li>
      <li>Open a new tab without saying so.</li>
    </ul></div>
  </div>
</section>
